description:
Design an edge detector that detects falling edges for each bit in a 16-bit input signal. On each positive clock edge, if a falling edge is detected (i.e., the current input bit is 0 while the previous input bit was 1) for the least significant bit, the corresponding bit in the output `anyedge` is set to the current 16-bit input value. This provides a mechanism to monitor transitions of input signals over time, particularly focusing on recognizing when bits switch from high to low.
