Design a circuit that performs an HSV color range masking operation. It checks whether the input hue (H), saturation (S), and value (V) fall within specified upper and lower bounds for each component. When all conditions are satisfied, the output (o) is set to HIGH, indicating that the color is within the desired range; otherwise, the output is set to LOW. The module utilizes combinational logic to evaluate these comparisons simultaneously.
module top_module(
    input [8:0] H,
    input [7:0] S,V,
    output reg o  
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [8:0] H,
    input [7:0] S,V,
    output reg o  
);reg [8:0] u_h, l_h;
reg [7:0] u_s,u_v,l_s,l_v;

always @(H,S,V) begin
    if (l_h <= H && H <= u_h && l_s <= S && S <= u_s && l_v <= V && V <= u_v) begin
        o <= 1'd1;
    end else begin
        o <= 1'd0;
    end
end
endmodule

